 Reads boards/<name>/board.json and the CSV file it names ("data", relative to the board's folder) and writes
 boards/<name>/index.html. Rows are grouped into sections by the "section" field and ordered by the earliest date
 in each section; sections whose date has passed go under one fold at the bottom.
+
+Optional, for a list of tasks rather than dated events (the events board uses none of these):
+  section.empty   heading for rows with a blank section field (default "Other")
+  section.order   "name": sections in name order, the blank one first, nothing folded by date
+  done_label      rows whose status is "done" leave their section and go under one fold with this label
+  column.date     true: the field is a date; rows sort by it, and open rows show "overdue" or "this week"
+  column.prefix   text put before the value, e.g. "waiting on "
 """
